{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nDiscovered while adding the compact-worker leg to doctor's lock census (ticket\nbemused-painted-worm / 8a0d-96ca-a60e-4da6, merged as 8874ec98c7c). Snapshot GC's\noperation-linked trigger (a3da2f4cce) added a stamped worker lock at\n`<snapshot-store>/gc/worker.lock` (`rebar._snapshot.gc_trigger._WORKER_LOCK_NAME`), the same\ndetached-background-worker shape as `.rebar/compact-worker.lock` — a lock most likely to be\nheld by a process an operator cannot find with `ps`. `doctor_locks.scan_locks` censuses only\ntracker-adjacent locks, so a snapshot-GC worker that died between acquire and release leaves\na stamped lock the one diagnostic built to answer \"who holds what\" cannot see.\n\n## Decision\n\nADD the leg. The two design questions the ticket raised resolve cleanly:\n\n1. **Staleness discipline IS the shared table.** `gc_trigger._acquire_worker_lock` uses\n   `rebar._store.stamped_lock.stamped_file_lock` (the consolidation from story\n   1cf6-f902-5bfa-438f), which writes the same v2 ownership stamp as the drain and\n   compact-worker locks and adjudicates reclaim via\n   `rebar._store.lock_owner.stamped_file_is_stale`. So doctor's existing\n   `_existence_report` — which decodes the v2 stamp and asks that same shared table — is\n   exactly the right reader, no new staleness heuristic.\n2. **Root derivation must be READ-ONLY.** The lock lives on the per-host snapshot store\n   (`rebar._snapshot.repo_snapshot.store_root()`, `$REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` or\n   `tempfile.gettempdir()`, dir `rebar-gate-snapshots`), NOT the tracker's `.rebar/`. But\n   `store_root()` mkdirs+chmods the root and `gc_trigger._gc_dir` mkdirs `<store>/gc/` as\n   side effects — a diagnostic pass must not create directories (the census's existing\n   read-only guarantee: probing must never create what it probes). So the leg needs a\n   non-creating derivation seam, added where each layer already owns its layout.\n\nA store that does not exist yet reports the leg `free` — for an existence lock the file IS\nthe lock, so an absent store trivially holds nothing; this matches how the drain and\ncompact-worker legs report an absent lock file, and the row's note says the store may not\nexist yet.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py`: add `peek_store_root() -> Path` — the same\n   base-resolution as `store_root()` (`config.resolve_gate_tmpdir()` or\n   `tempfile.gettempdir()`, joined with `_STORE_DIRNAME`) WITHOUT mkdir/chmod; refactor\n   `store_root()` to call it then create (behavior preserved).\n2. `src/rebar/_snapshot/gc_trigger.py`: hoist the `\"gc\"` dirname into a `_GC_DIRNAME`\n   constant used by `_gc_dir`, and add `worker_lock_probe_path() -> Path` returning\n   `peek_store_root() / _GC_DIRNAME / _WORKER_LOCK_NAME` with no directory creation —\n   gc_trigger owns the sidecar layout, so doctor does not re-derive it.\n3. `src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py`: add `LEG_SNAPSHOT_GC_WORKER = \"snapshot-gc-worker\"`\n   as a sixth leg in `scan_locks`, built by the existing `_existence_report` on\n   `worker_lock_probe_path()` (module imported lazily inside the leg lambda's scope so the\n   census does not import the snapshot subsystem at module import). Note text: \"no detached\n   snapshot-GC worker holds the snapshot store's worker lock (per-host store; may not exist\n   yet)\". Update the module docstring: five → six legs, and a paragraph on the snapshot leg's\n   DIFFERENT root (per-host store, not the tracker), same stamped shape/shared table.\n   `scan_locks(tracker)` keeps its signature; the new leg is per-host and ignores the tracker\n   argument — the docstring says so.\n4. `src/rebar/schemas/doctor.schema.json`: add `\"snapshot-gc-worker\"` to the leg-name enum.\n5. `tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py`:\n   - an autouse fixture pinning `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` to a per-test tmp dir, so the census's\n     new host-global leg cannot leak REAL host state into any test in the module (the\n     free-store census test and both doctor integration tests assert exact finding sets).\n   - update `test_a_free_store_reports_every_leg_and_no_finding` to six legs; assert the\n     snapshot leg is `free` with `holder is None` when the store does not exist, and that\n     scanning did NOT create the store directory (the read-only guarantee for the new\n     derivation).\n   - `_plant_snapshot_gc_lock` helper writing a v2 stamp at\n     `repo_snapshot.peek_store_root() / \"gc\" / \"worker.lock\"` (under the pinned tmp base);\n     mirror the compact-worker tests: live holder → held/info, dead holder → stale finding\n     via `lock_findings`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The snapshot-GC worker lock joins `rebar doctor`'s census as leg\n      `snapshot-gc-worker`, derived from the per-host snapshot-store root without creating\n      any directory.\n- [x] The leg reports held-for / holder / staleness like the other stamped legs, with tests\n      for held (live + dead holder) and free/absent store.\n- [x] The dead-holder case is a stale-lock finding; a live holder is information; an absent\n      store (or free lock) is no finding, and the doctor JSON schema admits the new leg name.\n\n## Verify\n- pytest tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py tests/unit/test_snapshot_gc_trigger.py tests/unit/snapshot/test_repo_snapshot.py -x -q  (repo_snapshot tests live where they live; adjust path if the module sits directly under tests/unit)\n- make lint; make typecheck; python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787394531433475001,"uuid":"5b3adc49-2fc3-490b-8441-cb77635f46ef"}